From ec3276019cca7c996cf55b2a53e893573227feef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:16:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cursor: stop defaulting grok to the fast tier

Cursor's catalog ships grok with fast=true already selected in the default
variant, and the wire-id picker only penalised the mismatch in one direction,
so grok-4.6 resolved to cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast for every caller. The fast
tier is a different serving that answers without prompt caching: a 31k prompt
came back with cache_read_tokens:0 on every turn, so the whole prompt was
billed fresh each time.

Drop a fast that came from the catalog default rather than from the caller,
keeping the rest of the default so the reasoning effort survives, and penalise
an unrequested fast wire id enough that the effort bonus cannot select one.
The -fast suffix still reaches the fast tier, and a model offered only as fast
still resolves.

Measured after the change: grok-4.6 goes out as cursor-grok-4.6-high and its
continuation turns read 31,104 of 31,323 prompt tokens from cache.
